186259480 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259480 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186258721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259480 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fed49f22-b423-5b9a-b990-ba7eb27d6825" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259647 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259647 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124276" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259647 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259647 #edb/ref 1071 "The affine transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nx=4u+7v+2,\\,y=u+2v+1.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ of $T$ is\n\n$$\nu=ax-7y+3,\\,v=by+cx-2,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259647 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4865ae47-4fd4-593e-a597-ec2a2d5aa88e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259647 #edb/ref 1074 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, writing our transformation in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4u+7v+2 \\\\ u+2v+1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4u+7v \\\\ u+2v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 4-7\\cdot 1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -7 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -7 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -7 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -7 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x-2 \\\\ y-1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\cdot (x-2)+(-7)\\cdot (y-1) \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (x-2)+4\\cdot (y-1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2x-7y+3 \\\\ 4y-x-2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ in coordinate form is\n\n$$\nu=2x-7y+3,\\,v=4y+(-1)x-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+4+(-1)=5.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186263005 #edb/ref 1080 "2x-y-5=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263005 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263005 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0029eb5c-a868-5b35-b213-3fa6e3a04a1d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263009 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{x-1}{4}=2-y=z-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263009 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263009 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "00dfea87-0564-54b8-b2ba-b85b9b81f898" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263024 #edb/ref 1080 "x-1=y-2=z-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263024 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263024 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "02bdc94f-aecb-598c-8c8e-fd84d09e16d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263068 #edb/ref 1080 "x-3y=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263068 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263068 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "076ccae2-d102-5ad8-b1c2-ac28978e3e97" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263257 #edb/ref 1080 "x-y-2=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263257 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263257 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1b3882de-2108-52bf-b5e1-4c3304b9a5c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263298 #edb/ref 1080 "x-3=\\frac{y-2}{2}=z-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [